invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: next_word adds the ring word eight places on where FIPS 180-4
  §6.4.2 step 1 adds W[t - 7], the word nine places on, so every schedule
  word past a block's sixteenth is wrong and so is every digest a host
  object computes under the library's own names. The index is inside the
  ring, so no memory check sees it. bin/sha2_equiv_test holds sha512.c's
  first arm to the second, which compresses on sha512_compress.c, and the
  first case differs.

--- old
    uint64_t word = kept(&ring[i]) + lower_sigma0(fifteen_back) + kept(&ring[(i + 9) & 15]) +
--- new
    uint64_t word = kept(&ring[i]) + lower_sigma0(fifteen_back) + kept(&ring[(i + 8) & 15]) +
